 "result": "In this repo the Flask names are renamed, so the decorator is `needs_app_scope`, not `with_appcontext`.\n\n- **Decorator:** `needs_app_scope` is in `src/tessel/cli.py:380`. It loads the app and pushes its app context around your callback.\n- **Easiest route:** register the command with `@app.cli.command()` or `@bundle.cli.command()`. Both are `AppGroup` instances (`src/tessel/app.py:338`, `src/tessel/bundles.py:49`), and `AppGroup.command` wraps the function in `needs_app_scope` for you. You only need to add the decorator yourself on a plain `click` command or group.\n- **Loader class:** `LaunchInfo` (`src/tessel/cli.py:293`) loads the app through `LaunchInfo.load_app()` (`src/tessel/cli.py:333`). `TesselGroup` (`src/tessel/cli.py:531`) calls it to discover the app's commands.",
